    {
      "key": "0x10",
      "name": "attribute mode control",
      "aliases": [
        "mode control register",
        "attribute controller mode"
      ],
      "regions": [
        {
          "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
          "lines": "3997-3999"
        },
        {
          "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
          "lines": "4018-4053"
        },
        {
          "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_attr.cpp",
          "function": "write_p3c0",
          "case": [
            "0x10"
          ]
        },
        {
          "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_attr.cpp",
          "function": "read_p3c1",
          "case": [
            "0x10"
          ]
        },
        {
          "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
          "lines": "4056-4060"
        },
        {
          "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_attr.cpp",
          "lines": "453"
        }
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "n": "1",
          "on": "is",
          "of": "doc",
          "text": "The Attribute Mode Control register is a read/write register at index hex 10, written at 03C0 and read at 03C1.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
              "lines": "3997-3999",
              "sha": "ea35c61125836627919797c5e568584476f999161f13222eabe6de9c8ccd6166"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "2",
          "on": "bit 7",
          "of": "doc",
          "text": "Bit 7 (PS) is stored; 0 takes P5 and P4 from the internal palette, 1 from Color Select bits 1 and 0 (capture reads `oof`).",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
              "lines": "4018-4024",
              "sha": "2ad3a5f273d6331d2df1e1be86ce5db4135fa7330eb6d3c5bfd4e100c1bfa404"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "3",
          "on": "bit 6",
          "of": "doc",
          "text": "Bit 6 (PW) is stored; the document samples the video data so 8 bits select a color in 256-color mode, and sets it to 0 in all other modes.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
              "lines": "4025-4028",
              "sha": "21f6ff47141296db3a30cd478f7016b42151465569f6ef53f57ae064f083fceb"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "4",
          "on": "bit 5",
          "of": "doc",
          "text": "Bit 5 (PP) is stored; the document forces pel panning to 0 from a successful line compare until the next vertical sync, and has no effect when 0.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
              "lines": "4029-4036",
              "sha": "a572615ece3808d7274f9c1ead374c70e9700a03aac3119e0e4f8ec0dec7f37e"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "5",
          "on": "bit 3",
          "of": "doc",
          "text": "Bit 3 (EB) is stored; the document has the attribute's most-significant bit select background intensity when 0 and blinking when 1.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
              "lines": "4037-4040",
              "sha": "2f05dd8f7d875845bb561c064235341b617c116ee74f51751a30c33f39c4314e"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "6",
          "on": "bit 2",
          "of": "doc",
          "text": "Bit 2 (ELG) is stored; the document makes the ninth dot equal to the background when 0 and enables line-graphics codes C0 through 0F in monochrome emulation when 1.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
              "lines": "4041-4049",
              "sha": "e5eb0cbfbe525d542a25753ea2d87683199bbaad65a42c29ad152542b72d6c4f"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "7",
          "on": "is",
          "of": "doc",
          "text": "For fonts that do not use the line-graphics codes the document advises setting bit 2 to 0.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
              "lines": "4050-4053",
              "sha": "35cf192e7e02586e06716061b3bb55ca5ac8b17fe23e3eed670a2ca5144bf150"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "8",
          "on": "bit 1",
          "of": "doc",
          "text": "Bit 1 (ME) is stored; the document selects monochrome emulation when it is 1 and color emulation when 0.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
              "lines": "4056-4058",
              "sha": "dc5c33dfd8db7fbae7dea3920b20b354fcc99402ea32e2e0777fac71dc3bca38"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "9",
          "on": "bit 0",
          "of": "doc",
          "text": "Bit 0 (G) is stored; the document selects the graphics mode when it is 1.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
              "lines": "4059-4060",
              "sha": "c1d62efd143e4c0038a2aa70ad4d2529ff30ca19d0f7334e02c62f848c71a9bc"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "10",
          "on": "read",
          "of": "doc",
          "text": "The register is read at port hex 03C1.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
              "lines": "3998-3999",
              "sha": "9046a290fac81c180e97058313aba12c6f314ff58c0f7df705f8d41a1518eac2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "101",
          "on": "bit 7",
          "of": "dosbox-x",
          "vs": "extra",
          "text": "A change of bit 7 makes DOSBox-X re-send all sixteen palette entries to the DAC.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_attr.cpp",
              "lines": "276-280",
              "sha": "830b792f3df356b77d56f673ab4123183a2300c01f8df3b4d5455301538f671f"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "102",
          "on": "bit 3",
          "of": "dosbox-x",
          "vs": "extra",
          "text": "A change of bit 3 calls VGA_SetBlinking with the bit.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_attr.cpp",
              "lines": "281-284",
              "sha": "5b596f33e44f595c4b73899f0cd5e5dc5f2d8f48666efda2d34d6aa88c213f45"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "103",
          "on": "bit 0",
          "of": "dosbox-x",
          "vs": "extra",
          "text": "A change of bits 0 or 6 calls VGA_DetermineMode and the odd-even complexity check, and that of bit 6 resizes the screen in the 256-color mode.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_attr.cpp",
              "lines": "286-291",
              "sha": "6ca25e9f069933b5c6b8f9bdc00a2bcf19b420a1d424db2f1f2a293837d7827a"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "104",
          "on": "bit 2",
          "of": "dosbox-x",
          "vs": "extra",
          "text": "A change of bit 2 recomputes a text mode's pel panning from the panning register, adding one for 9-dot characters.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_attr.cpp",
              "lines": "296-306",
              "sha": "291eb4b1ff7f3c86087fa48eb1306aaa2afedeef525b5d75d044d3ea8bc07bfe"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "105",
          "on": "write",
          "of": "dosbox-x",
          "vs": "extra",
          "text": "While emulating an EGA, only the low five bits of the value are kept before it is stored.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_attr.cpp",
              "lines": "272-274",
              "sha": "90fd09b46a10e9610a0d3f80652352d27b2cf744206d99583ba65a350895244e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "closed": [
